  data: {
    LLM: "Each of the 4 players must eventually play 5 'contracts' (3 negative, 2 positive):\n1. Negative Deals (No Trumps): Avoid taking any tricks, or specific cards like Hearts, Queens, or the King of Hearts.\n2. Positive Deals (Trumps): The dealer chooses the trump suit and tries to win as many tricks as possible.\n3. Turn Order: Standard Whist-style play. You must follow suit if possible.",
    Player: "Each of the 4 players must eventually play 5 'contracts' (3 negative, 2 positive):\n1. Negative Deals (No Trumps): Avoid taking any tricks, or specific cards like Hearts, Queens, or the King of Hearts.\n2. Positive Deals (Trumps): The dealer chooses the trump suit and tries to win as many tricks as possible.\n3. Turn Order: Standard Whist-style play. You must follow suit if possible.",
    objective: 'Finish the 20nddeal series with the highest positive score. Negative points from early rounds are offset by positive points from later rounds.',
